#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=9 nAlgorithms=6;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1793974111717'; [Fri Nov 06 15:08:31 CET 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[!Dusky dolphin (Lagenorhynchus obscurus) mitochondrial haplotypes from Cassens et al. (2003), Mol Ecol 12:1781-1792,
DOI 10.1046/j.1365-294x.2003.01876.x: 36 haplotypes over 60 variable sites, as distributed with SplitsTree.
RazorHaploNet with the Shave filter.]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.).
The original input consisted of 36 taxa and 36 DNA sequences of length 60.
The Razor Haplo Net method was used (default options) so as to obtain 55 nodes and 64 edges.
The Shave Filter method was used (default options) so as to obtain 51 nodes and 56 edges.

References:
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

